  "preamble": "De-retroflexion of the aspirated retroflex stop [ʈʰ] to the aspirated alveolar stop [tʰ] keeps the aspiration but moves the closure forward, removing the retroflex series. In Assamese the Indo-Aryan retroflex and dental stops merged into alveolars, so ঠ (ṭh) is pronounced /tʰ/ although the spelling keeps the old letter.",
